    description: "## Origin\n\nMaterialized 2026-06-04 from the 2026-06-03 fold-audit (Family M). Stand-alone finding F25.17 previously folded onto INV-numat. Full evidence on INV-numat's pass-25 discussion entry.\n\n## Symptom\n\n`profile.frameworks=['lit', 'starlette']` lists 2 frameworks declared as present on root substrate. No node-level reference to these frameworks exists — 0 nodes carry `meta.framework` or any provenance pointing back to the declared values.\n\nA consumer reading \"frameworks: starlette\" cannot trace WHERE in the codebase starlette is used; the framework name is a top-level declaration with no graph-level anchoring.\n\n## Invariant\n\nEvery framework listed in `profile.frameworks` has at least one node referring to it. Either:\n1. `node.meta.framework=<X>` for nodes that import or extend framework symbols.\n2. A separate `profile.framework_evidence: {<framework>: [list of node_ids]}` mapping.\n\nPath (1) leverages existing meta surface; path (2) is a separate provenance index.\n\n## Fix sketch\n\nProducer-side: framework detector that adds entries to `profile.frameworks` also populates `meta.framework` on framework-import / framework-extends nodes. OR: framework detector populates a separate `framework_evidence` mapping at top level.\n\n## Source provenance\n\n- **F25.17** — INV-numat discussion entry 2026-06-02 (pass-25 batch).\n\nLab notebook: pass 25.\n\n## Related rows\n\n- Parent: **INV-numat**.\n- Sibling: **WI-discovery-language-producer-migration** (Family M — adjacent producer-migration gap).\n- Family M siblings."  # 6372
